 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"55ef2e99-eba5-4bae-b92e-636e612e569d"],

Cell["1. Why model traffic?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"852bc9a2-d557-48a4-bf89-700c3eeabde3"],

Cell["\<\
Traffic engineers need quantitative tools to answer questions like: What \
happens to queue lengths on Union Street if we add a bus gate? If the Bridge \
of Don closes for maintenance, does Anderson Drive absorb the flow, or does \
half the city seize up? What is the shortest green phase for the busy \
intersection at Mounthooly that still keeps average delay under \
30\[ThinSpace]s? None of these questions has a closed-form answer, but all of \
them are tractable in simulation once the correct mathematical model has been \
picked for the right spatial scale.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"453320ee-5f3b-470c-9c76-392f20d1a064"],

Cell["\<\
There is no single \"right\" model of traffic; there is a hierarchy of \
models, each trading detail for tractability. At the coarsest end we treat \
traffic as a compressible fluid; at the finest end we simulate every vehicle \
with its own ODE. In between sit stochastic cellular automata and queueing \
approximations. This notebook introduces each of these scales, shows the \
canonical model for it, and ends by stitching them all together on the real \
Aberdeen street map.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"707625d5-64f7-4ba6-80fd-66cb608d4317"],

Cell["\<\
Aberdeen is a good running example for three reasons: it is small enough to \
be tractable (pop. ~200\[ThinSpace]000, compact historic centre), large \
enough to be interesting (international airport, oil-industry commuter flows, \
a peripheral ring road), and its geography creates natural bottlenecks \
\[LongDash] the two main river bridges, the Haudagain roundabout, the \
Anderson Drive corridor \[LongDash] that any model will want to reproduce.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a801aa89-3517-44b8-9bc8-96c5fb498398"],

Cell["2. The macroscopic view: the LWR model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c2e5b6b8-ff9f-4165-a001-be6b32d0feed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lighthill and Whitham (1955), followed independently by Richards (1956), \
proposed that traffic on a long road obeys the same conservation law as any \
other compressible one-dimensional fluid: vehicles cannot be created or \
destroyed, so the density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", "x", ",", " ", "t", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "2ba310c5-a788-433d-b759-0ec3381d4824"],
 " and flow ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "b2f78729-3f9a-4325-ba4b-a5566301e215"],
 " satisfy"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a6fd0c4-0dc7-481e-acc2-d35e3cd8e04e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "\[Rho]"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "t"}]], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
     RowBox[{"Q", "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}]}], 
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"356c1b12-a52a-4ed1-ae7a-b91a85090ef5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is a first-order hyperbolic PDE. The missing ingredient is the ",
 StyleBox["fundamental diagram",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " \[LongDash] an empirical relation between density and flow. The simplest, \
due to Greenshields (1935), is linear in the speed:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51a64b0a-29bf-47c5-86a3-5f0a759f45b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Q", "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["v", "max"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      FractionBox["\[Rho]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "max"]]}], ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"b3a65c4e-872d-41a8-904e-d436f063e348"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "so that flow is zero both at empty road (\[Rho]=0) and at bumper-to-bumper \
jam (\[Rho]=",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1f3dd8-6233-4293-a33b-2177b4b97b36"],
 "), and is maximised at the critical density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "c"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "max"], "/", "2"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ca8594ca-9814-4568-8522-458fdc5be32d"],
 ". Plugging this into the conservation law gives a nonlinear scalar PDE that \
develops shocks from smooth initial data: the mathematical origin of a \
traffic jam."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16340137-f3e8-4a9b-80cf-d48a12e8ad37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We discretise it with the Godunov finite-volume scheme (the simplest upwind \
flux that respects the shock structure). The numerical flux between cells \
with left density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "L"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "1e9819c5-8d1a-4feb-8314-ef288f13c5b6"],
 " and right density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "R"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "67b202dc-5f8f-40be-b192-f50002605686"],
 " is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd98206d-bdaa-42d3-be3d-471ca7f6742a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Q", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["", 
     RowBox[{"i", "+", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "G"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"if", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "L"], "\[LessEqual]", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "R"]}], ":", 
    RowBox[{"min", "(", 
     RowBox[{"Q", "(", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "L"], ")"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Q", "(", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "R"], ")"}], ",", " ", "Q", "(", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "c"], ")", ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"5d055f38-3ff6-44b5-9a9b-aa24a3f8363e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with the usual case analysis for \[Rho]\\[ThinSpace]L > \
\[Rho]\\[ThinSpace]R. A CFL condition (\[CapitalDelta]t \[LessEqual] \
\[CapitalDelta]x / ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["v", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ab31a550-6ab9-444b-b4c4-db20ee0b70b0"],
 ") keeps the scheme stable. The Wolfram implementation is a dozen lines:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7030bea6-c5c6-41e0-9439-fafcb7f74ee2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Greenshields", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "rhoMax_", ",", " ", "vMax_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"rho", " ", "vMax", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"rho", "/", "rhoMax"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GodunovFlux", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "rhoL_", ",", " ", "rhoR_", ",", " ", "rhoMax_", ",", " ", "vMax_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"rhoCrit", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"rhoMax", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"qL", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Greenshields", "[", 
         RowBox[{"rhoL", ",", " ", "rhoMax", ",", " ", "vMax"}], "]"}]}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"qR", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Greenshields", "[", 
         RowBox[{"rhoR", ",", " ", "rhoMax", ",", " ", "vMax"}], "]"}]}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Which", "[", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"rhoL", " ", "<=", " ", "rhoR"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{"Which", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"rhoL", " ", ">=", " ", "rhoCrit"}], ",", " ", "qL", ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"rhoR", " ", "<=", " ", "rhoCrit"}], ",", " ", "qR", ",", 
         "\n", "            ", "True", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Greenshields", "[", 
          RowBox[{"rhoCrit", ",", " ", "rhoMax", ",", " ", "vMax"}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", "True", ",", "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{"If", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"qL", " ", "<=", " ", "qR"}], ",", " ", "qL", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"If", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"rhoL", " ", ">=", " ", "rhoCrit"}], ",", " ", "qL", ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
            RowBox[{"qL", ",", " ", "qR"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e2de7c3d-ed5f-41b2-\
b217-9c1f959c2e30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Seeding an initial high-density block ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Rho]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "5ef1692a-afee-4093-b5e0-dc5524c07c52"],
 "=120 veh/km in the middle of an otherwise uniform road at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Rho]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "d8b273fc-383f-4372-aa31-62766e2c129e"],
 "=20 veh/km produces the canonical signature of an LWR jam: a \
backward-travelling shock (upstream boundary of the jam) and a downstream \
rarefaction fan (vehicles leaving the jam into free road)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fad5e37b-f5d1-401e-8bf4-32ee1b10f2aa"],

