Cell["9. Network-level assignment: Wardrop equilibrium", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3e0ad1aa-55e5-4f75-88ea-daa65d00658f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Zooming back out: at the scale of a whole city, the question is no longer \
\"what does one link look like?\" but \"how do drivers distribute themselves \
across the network?\". The standard answer is Wardrop's first principle \
(1952): at equilibrium, all used paths between the same origin-destination \
pair have equal cost; no driver can unilaterally improve by switching routes. \
Formally, for all paths ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "q"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "eae38d65-0079-4921-b2d8-32f128aa4ea3"],
 " used by the same OD pair,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dc490b75-10d8-400e-9b2c-2cea262f43e7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["c", "p"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["c", "q"], "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
   "\[ForAll]", " ", "used", " ", "paths", " ", "p", ",", " ", "q"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"5c135b92-10f0-4221-a934-54da8a4697fd"],

Cell["\<\
Beckmann (1956) showed that Wardrop equilibrium link flows are the unique \
minimiser of the convex program\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"275f39ea-6e00-415e-bfeb-5968ab972ec2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["min", "x"], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{"e", "\[Element]", "E"}], ""], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
     SubscriptBox["x", "e"]], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["t", "e"], "(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "\[Omega]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"2e0769bd-ed52-4d5c-9d66-a47360524d49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "e"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "25ca41e5-780b-481a-b4f6-de2ad97f13c4"],
 " is the flow on link ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["e", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ec232915-44d1-4cb2-bcb2-1197b693b4e4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["t", "e"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[CenterDot]", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "4bba1253-a66a-4ce5-8558-86402525405d"],
 " is the increasing link-cost function. The universal practical choice is \
the BPR formula of the US Bureau of Public Roads,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"461750a1-0cf5-4144-aa45-f033a153280f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["t", "e"], "(", 
    SubscriptBox["x", "e"], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["t", "e", "0"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"1", "+", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         FractionBox[
          SubscriptBox["x", "e"], 
          SubscriptBox["C", "e"]], ")"}], "\[Beta]"]}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"231d68ca-07e5-4b36-b427-4424af8cbb33"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["t", "e", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "3d7ec34b-39c5-4e94-89da-5c7eae570e12"],
 " the free-flow travel time, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "e"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ae7a2e25-8540-40be-9b78-b110baf0171e"],
 " the capacity, and tuning parameters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "=", "0.15"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "a33be9b1-1d74-472d-aa4e-d53a5771cc60"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "=", "4"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c8efbe39-e8cd-41af-8cfc-9e6e89127e80"],
 ". The objective is smooth and strictly convex, so ",
 StyleBox["FindMinimum", "Input"],
 " solves it in a handful of iterations."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1dbd386c-4015-4398-85b7-a50b4f1d2643"],

Cell["\<\
On a hand-curated 15-node Aberdeen network (Haudagain, Bridge of Don, Bridge \
of Dee, Union Street / Market Street, Anderson Drive, AWPR junction, etc.) \
with four origin-destination pairs summing to 8\[ThinSpace]500 veh/h, the \
solver identifies Union Street and Anderson Drive (south) as the dominant \
bottlenecks \[LongDash] saturation values of 3.0\[Times] and 2.4\[Times] \
capacity respectively, matching the real-world experience of commuters.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13915fa8-d840-4147-b6cd-b11ee019a525"],

